    {
      "id": "1532464097570848900",
      "type": "Reply",
      "timestamp": "2026-07-30T19:05:12.667+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": "2026-07-30T19:08:09.548+00:00",
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "The `gf180mcu_ocd_io` SRAM macro targets 3.3V and the `gf180mcu_fd_ip_sram` 5V. \nYou might be able to use them at different voltages but you will want to check that. \nBy default template assumes you are working at 5V. \nAs for if the SRAM has been silicon proven **you will want to confirm** with others but I think the answer is yes.\n\n@Tim Edwards would you be so kind as to confirm that the `gf180mcu_ocd_io` SRAMs you sent out as part of ws1 are working as intended ?",
      "author": {
        "id": "509798510170865675",
        "name": "essen__",
        "discriminator": "0000",
